    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "Use of Proceeds We may receive up to $10,002,750\n    in aggregate gross proceeds from this offering, consisting of: (i) $2,750 upon exercise of the Warrant in full at exercise price\n    of $0.01 per share, and (ii) up to $10,000,000 upon sales of Put Shares by us to the Investor at $2.00 per share. We intend to use\n    the net proceeds that we receive for general corporate purposes. See \u201cUse of Proceeds\u201d for additional information. Nasdaq Capital Market Ticker Symbol Our Common Stock is listed\n    on the Nasdaq Capital Market under the symbol \u201cGOAI.\u201d Risk Factors An investment in our Common\n    Stock involves a high degree of risk. See the section entitled \u201cRisk Factors\u201d included in this prospectus supplement,\n    the accompanying base prospectus and our Annual Report on Form 10-K for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2025, incorporated by\n    reference herein, and any other risk factor",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "Risk Factors An investment in our Common\n    Stock involves a high degree of risk. See the section entitled \u201cRisk Factors\u201d included in this prospectus supplement,\n    the accompanying base prospectus and our Annual Report on Form 10-K for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2025, incorporated by\n    reference herein, and any other risk factors described in the documents incorporated by reference herein, for a discussion of certain\n    factors to consider carefully before deciding to invest in our Common Stock. Field: Page; Sequence: 11; Value: 1 S- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo 9 Field: /Sequence Field: /Page The\nnumber of shares of our Common Stock to be outstanding after this offering is based on 40,515,433 shares of our Common Stock outstanding\nas of October 13, 2026, and excludes: \u25cf 30,000,000 shares of Common\n    Stock issuable upon conversion of 200,000 outstanding sha",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION If\nyou invest in our Common Stock, your interest will be diluted to the extent of the difference between the assumed offering price per\nshare and the pro forma as adjusted net tangible book value per share of Common Stock immediately after this offering. The\npurchase price per Put Share in this offering is $2.00 pursuant to the Purchase Agreement. As\nof June 30, 2026, our net tangible book value was approximately $16,655,784, or $0.42 per share of Common Stock. Our net tangible book\nvalue per share represents the amount of our total tangible assets (which excludes capitalized website development costs and other intangibles,\nunamortized original issue discount and deferred financing costs) reduced by the amount of our total liabilities and divided by the total\nnumber of shares of our Common Stock outstanding as of June 30, 2026. After\ngiving effect to the sale of all 5,000,000 Pu",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
